// Golden lockstep replay that pins two phase orders of `SimWorld::step_into` (Phase 9 §9 gap 4).
//
// The broad replay (golden_replay.ron) stays green when either of these orders is swapped:
//   1. `update_vision` before `acquire_targets`: a unit acquires a target on the very tick a
//      spotter reveals it, not one tick later;
//   2. route upkeep before the arrival decision (`MotionDraft::walk`): a unit whose route was
//      dropped mid-order is routed again before its arrival is judged, so an empty route is not
//      mistaken for a last leg.
// This script makes each swap change the world checksum within ten ticks of the situation, and
// records a checksum every 10 ticks so a divergence is reported close to where it starts.
// Recorded on 2026-11-04 against unmodified simulation code; under the vision swap it diverges
// at checkpoint 6 (ticks 61 to 70), under the upkeep swap at checkpoint 25 (ticks 251 to 260).
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-04-combat-sc2-alignment WP2 (Q0036, D-3): "blue_spotter" has a
// damage point of 0 and now fires every 20 ticks, its period, from tick 121 instead of every
// 21 from tick 122, so checkpoints 13 to 31 (ticks 121 to 310) changed; the rest did not.
// The swap checkpoints above were measured on the first recording and not re-measured; the
// spotter's shots touch neither situation, and the test still finds both in the replay.
// Re-recorded for WP6 (Q0038) and for WP7 (Q0039): "blue_line" and "blue_column" (pulse_bot)
// now walk at 0.126 per tick (was 0.09), so checkpoints 3 to 60 (from ticks 21 to 30, the
// first after the column's move order at tick 20) changed. The ticks named in the scenario
// below are those of the first recording; the column now reaches the choke sooner. The test
// still finds both situations in the replay.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-04-battle-flipbook-animation WP2 (checksum schema 9 -> 10): each
// entity's `anim_progress`, a constant zero no system wrote, is no longer encoded, so every
// checkpoint changed. No behaviour did: the render snapshots of all 600 ticks are byte for byte
// those of schema 9.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-04-combat-sc2-alignment WP9 (D-4): a new entity's
// `ticks_since_last_damage` starts at u16::MAX instead of 250, and that counter is hashed, so
// every checkpoint changed. No behaviour did: with the spawn value left at 250, every
// checkpoint stays as recorded for flipbook WP2.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-04-combat-sc2-alignment WP16 (Q0045 4b, D-10): "blue_spotter"
// (`flying_saucer`) is now the Phoenix: no ground weapon, speed 0.238 (was 0.15), sight 10 (was
// 11), energy 200 (was 0). Every checkpoint changed: its energy is hashed from spawn, it flies
// from tick 10 at the new speed and reaches the ledge 19 ticks sooner, and it no longer shoots
// the zealots on the ledge (before: 9 shots, ticks 121 to 281), so "blue_line" alone kills
// them. The survivor count at tick 600 (27) is unchanged, and the test still finds both
// situations (the reveal and acquisition 19 ticks sooner; the repaths at the same ticks).
// Re-recorded for WP12 group S1 (Q0039): "blue_armor" (rhino_beetle) walks at 0.126 per tick
// (was 0.09, the Normal-time speed). Checkpoints 1 and 2 are unchanged; from checkpoint 3
// (ticks 21 to 30), when it starts its first Move at tick 20, every checkpoint changed. The
// test still finds both situations.
// Re-recorded for WP17 commit f (Q0045 1b): every hull turns at its StarCraft II rate (55.99
// degrees per tick for pulse_bot, rhino_beetle and psi_grey, 84.00 for flying_saucer; was
// instant), so units turning to a new path or target face it a few ticks later. Checkpoints 1 to
// 4 (ticks 1 to 40) are unchanged; from checkpoint 5 (ticks 41 to 50) most checkpoints changed.
// The test still finds both situations.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP3 d (B-34): "blue_spotter"
// (flying_saucer) spawns with the Phoenix's EnergyStart, 50 (was its maximum, 200; liberty
// UnitData:3727). A unit's energy is hashed, so every checkpoint changed from checkpoint 1. No
// behaviour did: nothing in the replay spends energy, and with energy left out of the checksum
// every checkpoint equals that of the commit before.
//
// Scenario, on the shipped default arena. In world coordinates (map rows are stored north
// first): low ground at y < 30, an abyss band at y = 30..33 crossed only by the ramp at
// x = 30..33, high ground at y >= 34.
//   - "red_ledge" holds position on the high-ground lip, five world units above "blue_line" on
//     the low ground. The cliff hides it from blue, so blue cannot fire.
//   - "blue_spotter", an air unit, flies in over the abyss. On the tick its sight reaches the
//     ledge (tick 64 when recorded, 45 since WP16), "blue_line" acquires (same-tick reveal and acquisition) and shoots the
//     ledge down.
//   - "blue_column" and "blue_armor" (twenty bodies, two sizes) are sent to one point just past
//     the top of the ramp, jam in the four-cell choke, and units at the foot of the ramp stall
//     and drop their routes while friends ahead already stand on the goal (the first, at tick
//     252). The group then moves on across the plateau and back down through the same choke.
// tests/golden_replay_tests.rs checks from the replay that both situations still occur.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP4 (B-11, checksum schema 10 -> 11): each
// entity's `previous_target_position`, where its automatic target last stood, is hashed, so every
// checkpoint changed. No behaviour did: no rule writes the field yet, so it is `None` for every
// entity on every tick, and the encoding only gains its empty tag.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-04-combat-sc2-alignment WP14 Amendment 7 (Q0057, B-12): scan
// ranges are measured edge to edge and take StarCraft II's reference values, "blue_line" and
// "blue_column" (pulse_bot) 5.5 (was 9, centre to centre). On tick 45, when the spotter reveals
// the ledge, "blue_line" marine 6 no longer acquires "red_ledge" zealot 28, 6.40 between centres
// and 5.53 beyond both edges; the other five marines still do (same-tick reveal and acquisition
// holds). Checkpoints 1 to 4 are unchanged; from checkpoint 5 (ticks 41 to 50) every checkpoint
// changed. The test still finds both situations.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP5 (B-2, checksum schema 11 -> 12): each
// weapon's `strike_interval_ticks` and `followup_max_distance`, each entity's `pending_strikes`
// and each projectile's `strikes` are hashed, so every checkpoint changed. No behaviour did: every
// shipped interval is 0, so every strike still lands on its release tick, and with the four
// fields left out of the encoding (schema 11) both fixtures reproduce as recorded for the scan
// ranges (Q0057).
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP6 (B-14, checksum schema 12 -> 13): each
// weapon's Armored and Light bonuses are replaced by its bonus against every attribute, encoded
// as eight values, so every checkpoint changed. No behaviour did: with the bonuses encoded as the
// two former fields at schema 12, both fixtures reproduce as recorded for WP5.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP7 (B-15): a strike that breaks the shields
// sends the shield-mitigated damage minus the shields to life (was raw x (1 - shields / mitigated)).
// With shield armour 0, as for every "red_ledge" (psi_grey) zealot here, the two are equal in real
// numbers; the old quotient lost about 1e-9 of life to fixed-point rounding at each break.
// Checkpoints 7 to 12 and 16 to 34 (ticks 61 to 120 and 151 to 340) changed, while a zealot
// carried that rounding; see golden_replay.ron for the proof that nothing else did.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP8a (B-16, checksum schema 13 -> 14): a
// splash's three fixed radii become its list of zones (radius and fraction), so the schema byte
// changes every checkpoint. No behaviour did: with the zones encoded at schema 13, both fixtures
// reproduce as recorded for WP7 (no splash weapon is encoded in either replay's state).
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP8b (B-18, checksum schema 14 -> 15): each
// splash also encodes its shape (a circle, or a line's origin, axis and offsets), so the schema
// byte changes every checkpoint. No behaviour did: with the shape encoded at schema 14, both
// fixtures reproduce as recorded for WP8a.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP9 group g10 (B-47): "blue_armor"
// (rhino_beetle) sees 9 (was 10, StarCraft II 5.0.14 `liberty` UnitData:7210). What the squad sees
// is world state from tick 1, so every checkpoint changed. With only the Roach analogue's sight
// restored to 10, both fixtures reproduce as recorded for WP8b.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP9 group g12 (B-47): collision radii as
// StarCraft II 5.0.14 (`CUnit` `Radius`): "blue_armor" (rhino_beetle) 0.5 (was 0.5625, the class
// default `core` UnitData:41) and "red_siege" (railgun_crawler) 0.875 (was 0.75, `liberty`
// UnitData:5094). Radii are part of the hashed bodies, so checkpoints 1 to 60 (ticks 1 to 600)
// changed; from checkpoint 61 on they are those of group g10 again. With only
// those two radii restored, both fixtures reproduce as recorded for WP9 group g10.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP9 (B-82, checksum schema 15 -> 16): each
// weapon also encodes its structure strike (none on any weapon here), so the encoding changes
// every checkpoint. No behaviour did: no shipped weapon has a structure strike yet, and the whole
// matrix and battle 33 are bit-identical to WP9 group g12.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP10 (B-29, checksum schema 16 -> 17): each
// weapon's acquisition arc and each unit's engaged target are encoded, so every checkpoint
// changed. No behaviour did: with the two fields left out of the encoding at schema 16, every
// checkpoint stays as recorded for WP9 (the shipped acquisition arcs equal the engaged arcs).
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP10 (B-29): every shipped weapon takes its
// StarCraft II acquisition arc, `Arc` / 2 (0 for every weapon that sets no `Arc`), so a unit faces
// a new target exactly before its first swing. `golden_replay` differs from checkpoint index 3
// (ticks 151 to 200) and `golden_replay_orders` from index 4 (ticks 41 to 50), the first fights;
// with the acquisition arcs set back to the engaged arcs both reproduce as recorded for the schema
// 17 commit.
// Re-recorded for WP10 (B-30, checksum schema 17 -> 18): each weapon's turret idle behaviour and
// rate are encoded, so every checkpoint changed. No behaviour did: with the field left out of the
// encoding at schema 17, every checkpoint stays as recorded for the B-29 data (every shipped
// turret holds).
// Re-recorded for WP11 (B-3, checksum schema 18 -> 19): each weapon's random delay range and each
// unit's carried delay are encoded, so every checkpoint changed. No behaviour did: with the fields
// left out of the encoding at schema 18, every checkpoint stays as recorded for the B-30 data
// (every shipped weapon authors no delay yet).
// Re-recorded for WP11 (B-3 data): every weapon adds StarCraft II's random delay of -0.0625 to
// 0.125 Normal s (-1.1161 to 2.2321 ticks, core WeaponData:35-36) to each attack, drawn from the
// world's seeded generator. The first checkpoint whose ticks hold a release changes (here and in
// the other fixture), and every later one; with the delays at (0.0, 0.0) both fixtures reproduce
// as recorded for schema 19.
// Re-recorded for WP12 (B-39 acceleration data): each unit gains at most its StarCraft II
// Acceleration per tick (Normal x 1.4^2 / 25^2; the Phoenix's 3.25, liberty UnitData:3686, is
// 0.010192 per tick squared; ground combat units keep 1000, instant). "blue_spotter"
// (flying_saucer) now starts its first move from rest, so checkpoint 1 (ticks 11 to 20) and every
// later one changed; with the archetypes' acceleration at their max_speed (instant) the fixture
// reproduces as recorded for the B-3 data.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-09-sc2-pathfinding WP2+WP3 (B-99, B-100, checksum schema 20 ->
// 21): each unit's `corner_round` is hashed, so every checkpoint changed. Behaviour first differs
// on tick 120 (checkpoint 12, ticks 111 to 120): "blue_column" unit 17 no longer holds
// (32.92, 29.37), the point the removed corner rewrite had put in place of its ramp corner
// because the column stood on it; it passes the corner and heads for its goal (32, 37). Units 8
// and 18 beside it move differently in contact on the same tick. The test still finds both
// situations.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-09-sc2-pathfinding WP4 (B-101): a corner waypoint is offset by the
// unit's own radius plus 0.05. "blue_armor" (rhino_beetle, radius 0.5) turns the ramp corner at
// (33.61, 29.61) in place of (33.70, 29.70) from its first route on tick 21, so checkpoints 1 and
// 2 are unchanged and from checkpoint 3 (ticks 21 to 30) every checkpoint changed. With the tier
// offset restored, every checkpoint equals that of WP2+WP3. The test still finds both situations.
